# =============================================================================
# model_manifest.env — per-model input contract for the benchmark suite.
#
# Copy this file to model_manifest.env (next to run_bench.sh) and fill it
# in when the model arrives. It is SOURCED BY BASH (build_model_engines.sh and
# run_bench.sh), so:
#   - every path must be ABSOLUTE, or computed inside this file (e.g. from
#     $HOME or a MODEL_ROOT you define at the top) — stages run from
#     different working directories and relative paths will break;
#   - values with spaces must be quoted;
#   - plain KEY=value lines only — this is not YAML.
#
# Fields marked REQUIRED are validated field-by-field by the engines stage,
# which dies naming the first missing one. Everything else may be left empty.
# Tensor-level detail (input names/shapes/dtypes, output tolerances) lives in
# the accuracy manifest JSON pointed to by ACC_MANIFEST — do not duplicate it
# here.
# =============================================================================

# Optional convenience root — define once, reuse below.
# MODEL_ROOT="$HOME/repos/mymodel"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_NAME  (REQUIRED for the engines stage)
# What:  short snake_case identifier for the model. Names the engines
#        (<name>_<prec>.engine, <name>_fp32_ref.engine), the mix manifest
#        the engines stage writes (mix_<device>_<name>.csv) and the results
#        directory (results_<device>_<name>).
# Units: none (identifier).
# From:  the model repo / mix document; pick once and never change mid-run.
# Example: MODEL_NAME=depth_model
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_NAME=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_REPO_URL  (optional — provenance only)
# What:  URL of the source repository the checkpoint/ONNX came from. Recorded
#        in provenance; never fetched by the kit.
# Units: URL string.
# From:  wherever the model team publishes it.
# Example: MODEL_REPO_URL=https://github.com/<org>/<model-repo>
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_REPO_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_CHECKPOINT  (optional — provenance only)
# What:  path or identifier of the trained checkpoint the ONNX was exported
#        from (commit hash, weights file, release tag). Recorded in
#        provenance so a number can be traced to exact weights.
# Units: free-form string / absolute path.
# From:  the model team's release notes.
# Example: MODEL_CHECKPOINT="$MODEL_ROOT/weights/epoch120.pt"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_CHECKPOINT=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_ONNX  (REQUIRED for the engines stage)
# What:  absolute path to the ONNX file. Both the quantized candidate engine
#        AND the fp32 reference engine are built from this same file — that
#        identity is what makes the accuracy gate meaningful.
# Units: absolute path to a .onnx file.
# From:  model repo export (dvc pull on a corp-network machine if tracked).
# Example: MODEL_ONNX="$MODEL_ROOT/onnx/model_fused.onnx"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_ONNX=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_PRECISION  (REQUIRED for the engines stage)
# What:  target precision of the candidate engine. One of: fp16 int8 fp8 fp32.
#        Maps to trtexec flags: fp16 -> --fp16; int8 -> --int8 --fp16
#        (+ --calib= if MODEL_CALIB_CACHE set); fp8 -> --fp8 --fp16;
#        fp32 -> no precision flags. Also selects which measured tensor
#        ceiling the budgets use.
# Units: enum string.
# From:  the quantization level decided for the deployment candidate.
# Example: MODEL_PRECISION=int8
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_PRECISION=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_CALIB_CACHE  (optional; int8 only)
# What:  absolute path to the INT8 calibration cache. Without it an int8
#        build is timing-valid but numerically meaningless — the accuracy
#        gate WILL fail, and that failure is real evidence, not noise.
# Units: absolute path to the cache file.
# From:  committed per-TRT-version caches in the model repo (portable across
#        TRT versions — affects accuracy fidelity only, never timing).
# Example: MODEL_CALIB_CACHE="$MODEL_ROOT/calibration_cache/10.3/calib.bin"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_CALIB_CACHE=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_PLUGINS  (optional)
# What:  absolute path to a custom TensorRT plugin .so, or empty if the model
#        needs none. Passed as --staticPlugins= on every trtexec invocation
#        (builds, timing, accuracy runs, NCU).
# Units: absolute path to one .so file.
# From:  build the repo's plugin library on THIS device with the device's
#        CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES (e.g. 120 on a Blackwell discrete card, 110 on a compute-capability-11.0 Jetson module).
# Example: MODEL_PLUGINS="$MODEL_ROOT/libs/tensorrt_plugins/build/libplugins.so"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_PLUGINS=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_SHAPES  (optional; required if the ONNX has dynamic dimensions)
# What:  input shapes in trtexec --shapes syntax. Dynamic dims left unpinned
#        are a hard error in the accuracy chain, so pin everything here.
#        Also parsed into --shape flags for the automatic arch-GFLOPs count.
# Units: trtexec syntax: name:AxBxC, comma-separated for multiple inputs.
# Example: MODEL_SHAPES="left:1x3x480x640,right:1x3x480x640"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_SHAPES=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_EXTRA_ARGS  (optional)
# What:  extra trtexec arguments appended to every invocation (builds and
#        runs) — layer-precision pins, tactic sources, format constraints.
#        Note: --warmUp takes MILLISECONDS.
# Units: space-separated trtexec flags, quoted as one string.
# Example: MODEL_EXTRA_ARGS="--layerPrecisions=disp_out:fp32"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_EXTRA_ARGS=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_SAMPLE_DIR  (optional; strongly recommended)
# What:  directory of real sample inputs from the model repo, referenced by
#        the accuracy manifest's per-input "samples" lists. With no samples
#        the battery falls back to seeded-random inputs — the run still
#        gates, but is stamped inputs_source:"seeded-random" (weaker
#        evidence, labeled as such in the results).
# Units: absolute directory path.
# Example: MODEL_SAMPLE_DIR="$MODEL_ROOT/samples"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_SAMPLE_DIR=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ACC_MANIFEST  (REQUIRED for the gate stage)
# What:  absolute path to the accuracy manifest JSON (acc_manifest_<model>.json)
#        declaring inputs (name/shape/dtype/kind/layout/range/samples), paired
#        input groups, output tolerances and the gate rule. See GUIDELINE.md
#        section "The two manifest contracts" for the field table.
# Units: absolute path to a .json file.
# Example: ACC_MANIFEST=${KIT_ROOT}/scripts/manifests.local/acc_manifest_mymodel.json
#   (write configs/manifests/acc_manifest_mymodel.json with ${INPUTS_ROOT}-based sample
#    paths; configure.sh expands it into scripts/manifests.local/)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ACC_MANIFEST=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_HZ  (REQUIRED for the engines stage)
# What:  the frame rate this model must sustain, from the frozen mix
#        definition — never a guess. Feeds bandwidth demand (bytes/frame x Hz)
#        and the Score term (arch GFLOPs x Hz).
# Units: frames per second.
# Rate not decided yet (generative rows): put a placeholder and say so in a
#        comment. Generative and end-to-end rows are additionally scored at
#        1/2/5/10/20/30 with the period as the deadline (report: rate sweep,
#        results.json: solo.N_vs_hz, solo.max_hz_at_N1) so the verdict can be
#        read off once the rate is fixed. The headline N uses this field.
# Example: MODEL_HZ=30
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_HZ=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_DEADLINE_MS  (REQUIRED for the engines stage)
# What:  per-frame latency deadline from the frozen mix definition. L =
#        deadline / p99; changing it re-baselines the mix — record why.
# Units: milliseconds.
# Example: MODEL_DEADLINE_MS=33.3
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_DEADLINE_MS=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_ARCH_GFLOPS  (optional; empty = computed automatically)
# What:  architectural GFLOPs per frame — the naive graph count at deployment
#        input size, FMA = 2. This is the Score's workload constant. Leave
#        empty and the engines stage runs compute_arch_gflops.py on
#        MODEL_ONNX (using MODEL_SHAPES) and fills it in. Never use
#        profiler-measured FLOPs here — those differ per device and belong
#        in diagnostics, not the Score.
# Units: GFLOPs (billions of floating-point ops per frame).
# Example: MODEL_ARCH_GFLOPS=17.09
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_ARCH_GFLOPS=

# =============================================================================
# REGISTRATION FIELDS (stage 4: register -> build -> measure -> N)
#
# One file per model: configs/manifests/model_manifest_<name>.env. The stage
# reads EVERY such file (via model_bench/registry.py) and builds/measures every
# declared builder x precision. Everything below is optional; leaving all of
# it empty means "one TensorRT engine from MODEL_ONNX at MODEL_PRECISION,
# timed with trtexec" - exactly the single-model behaviour.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_BUILDERS  (optional; default trt)
# What:  which stack produces the measured artifact. Comma-separated, ordered:
#          trt      TensorRT engine(s) from ONNX via trtexec (build_model_engines.sh)
#          adopt    an engine the model repo already built (MODEL_ENGINE); no build
#          edgellm  TensorRT Edge-LLM: quantize -> export -> llm_build/visual_build
#          trtllm   TensorRT-LLM: hf_ptq checkpoint dir (no .engine - by design)
#        Every entry is built and measured as its own row. An entry AFTER a
#        non-trt builder is a fallback target: it fires only if the declared
#        builder fails AND MODEL_ONNX is set; the row then records
#        builder_requested vs builder_used.
#        Platform rule (validated, a mismatch is a hard error, never a warning):
#          jetson   trt adopt edgellm      (trtllm does not target Jetson)
#          discrete trt adopt trtllm       (the discrete runtime of record is
#                                           TensorRT-LLM; edgellm is refused)
#        Use MODEL_BUILDERS_jetson / MODEL_BUILDERS_discrete to declare per
#        platform from ONE manifest (the platform-specific field wins).
# Example: MODEL_BUILDERS_jetson=edgellm
#          MODEL_BUILDERS_discrete=trtllm
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_BUILDERS=
MODEL_BUILDERS_jetson=
MODEL_BUILDERS_discrete=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_PRECISIONS  (optional; default = MODEL_PRECISION)
# What:  every precision to build and measure, comma-separated. One artifact
#        set and one measured row per entry. MODEL_PRECISION stays the PRIMARY
#        one: its row is named <name>; the others are <name>_<prec>.
#        Values: fp32 fp16 int8 fp8 nvfp4 nvfp4_nvflags (the last two are
#        generative-only).
# Example: MODEL_PRECISIONS=int8,fp16
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_PRECISIONS=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_ENGINE_SET  (optional; TensorRT multi-graph models only)
# What:  the member names of a model that is several ONNX graphs run in
#        sequence (an ASR model: encoder,decoder_first,decoder_past). Each member
#        gets its own ONNX (MODEL_ONNX_<member>), optional build flags
#        (MODEL_BUILD_FLAGS_<member>: shape profiles etc.; "@file" reads them
#        from a file), optional run flags (MODEL_RUN_FLAGS_<member>) and
#        optional MODEL_ARCH_GFLOPS_<member>. Engines land flat as
#        <engine_dir>/<member>_<prec>.engine, which is the layout an
#        end-to-end driver loads. Every member is also timed on its own
#        (row <name>_<member>).
# Example: MODEL_ENGINE_SET=encoder,decoder_first,decoder_past
#          MODEL_ONNX_encoder=${ONNX_DIR}/asr/encoder_model.onnx
#          MODEL_BUILD_FLAGS_encoder=--shapes=input_features:1x128x3000
#          MODEL_BUILD_FLAGS_decoder_past=@${KIT_ROOT}/configs/shapes/asr_decoder_past.flags
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_ENGINE_SET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_BUILD_ARGS  (optional; single-engine trt builds)
# What:  BUILD-ONLY trtexec flags (min/opt/max shape profiles for a dynamic
#        graph, say). They shape the artifact, so they enter the build stamp,
#        but they never ride a timing run - the built engine's own profile
#        does. MODEL_EXTRA_ARGS, by contrast, rides builds AND runs.
#        "@file" reads the flags from a file (comment lines starting with #
#        and line breaks are folded to single spaces) - use it for the long
#        per-tensor shape lists that do not fit on one manifest line.
#        Quoting: a value with spaces must be quoted as one string; the
#        manifest is sourced by bash (set -e), so an unquoted value with
#        spaces fails the registration instead of silently dropping the tail.
# Example: MODEL_BUILD_ARGS=@${KIT_ROOT}/configs/shapes/<name>.flags
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_BUILD_ARGS=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_ENGINE  (adopt builder; single engine)   MODEL_ENGINE_<member> (per member)
# What:  absolute path of an engine built OUTSIDE the kit (the model repo's own
#        builder, with its plugins and calibration). Adopted as-is; the row
#        records adopted:true and, when present, the repo's *_profile.json.
# Example: MODEL_ENGINE=${MODEL_ROOT}/depth_model/tensorrt/<gpu>/<trt version>/depth_model_int8.engine
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_ENGINE=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_ENGINE_DIR  (optional; default ${ENGINE_ROOT}/<device_tag>/<name>)
# What:  where this model's built artifacts live. Set it to reuse a workspace
#        that already holds valid engines (an Edge-LLM workspace with
#        engines_<prec>/llm, engines/visual); the build step re-validates them
#        and skips what is already stamped.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_ENGINE_DIR=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL_E2E_SRC  (optional; enables the end-to-end row <name>_e2e)
# What:  a C++ driver that runs the WHOLE model (all engines, the real loop)
#        and writes one JSON line per request. The kit compiles it and calls
#        the fixed contract:
#          <bin> <engine_dir> <precision> <MODEL_E2E_INPUTS> <out.jsonl> <repeats> 0 [MODEL_E2E_ARGS]
#        Required JSONL fields: gpu_total_ms (the latency of record for the
#        e2e row), ttft_ms, decode_ms_p99, wall_ms; optional: encoder_ms,
#        n_tokens, seconds, rtf_wall. The driver loads
#        <engine_dir>/<member>_<precision>.engine.
# Example: MODEL_E2E_SRC=${KIT_ROOT}/scripts/model_bench/cpp/asr_e2e.cpp
#          MODEL_E2E_INPUTS=${INPUTS_ROOT}/asr/mel_bin/list.txt
#          MODEL_E2E_REPEATS=3
#          MODEL_E2E_HZ=0            # 0 = not a sustained rate; N is the verdict
#          MODEL_E2E_DEADLINE_MS=    # empty = clip length (real-time factor 1.0)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_E2E_SRC=
MODEL_E2E_INPUTS=
MODEL_E2E_ARGS=
MODEL_E2E_REPEATS=
MODEL_E2E_HZ=
MODEL_E2E_DEADLINE_MS=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generative (edgellm / trtllm) fields
# MODEL_CHECKPOINT      REQUIRED here: the HF checkpoint DIRECTORY (config.json
#                       + safetensors) the stack quantizes and exports from.
# MODEL_LLM_BATTERY     edgellm: request json for the end-to-end llm_inference
#                       run (image paths inside it resolve from EDGELLM_ROOT).
# MODEL_LLM_IMAGE       trtllm: one image for the VLM step sweep.
# MODEL_LLM_CHUNK       decode tokens per step (default 8): the step the
#                       deadline judges = visual + prefill(reuse) + CHUNK x decode
# MODEL_LLM_CONTEXT_LEN prefill length (default 1024); MODEL_LLM_REUSE_LEN the
#                       KV prefix reused by the "prefill_reuse" measurement
#                       (default 896, i.e. 128 new tokens on a 1024 context)
# MODEL_LLM_MAX_INPUT_LEN engine build cap (default 4096)
# MODEL_LLM_VISUAL      0 for a text-only model (default 1: build/measure the
#                       vision encoder too)
# MODEL_LLM_BUILD_FLAGS  extra engine-build flags for the generative stack
#                       (Edge-LLM llm_build: --maxBatchSize, --maxInputLen,
#                       --maxKVCacheCapacity, --maxKVPoolPages ...). They enter
#                       the build stamp, so changing them triggers a rebuild.
# MODEL_LLM_BUILD_FLAGS_<prec>  the same, for ONE precision only (overrides
#                       the generic value for that precision). Quote the value.
# MODEL_HZ / MODEL_DEADLINE_MS apply to the STEP row (e.g. 10 Hz / 100 ms).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL_LLM_BATTERY=
MODEL_LLM_IMAGE=
MODEL_LLM_CHUNK=
MODEL_LLM_CONTEXT_LEN=
MODEL_LLM_REUSE_LEN=
MODEL_LLM_MAX_INPUT_LEN=
MODEL_LLM_VISUAL=
MODEL_LLM_BUILD_FLAGS=
